# {{name}}

A Pterodactyl panel theme that extends {{parentName}}, scaffolded by `p:extension:make --theme --extends={{parent}}`.
Everything this theme leaves out is {{parentName}}'s: its views, skins, stylesheet and settings. The themes guide,
`node_modules/@pterodactyl/sdk/THEMES.md`, covers each layer under "Building on another theme".

| To | Edit |
| --- | --- |
| Retune {{parentName}}'s colours, fonts, radius or spacing | `src/theme.css`, after the import |
{{viewsRow}}| Replace one of its settings, such as a new default | `extension.json`: the setting under the same name, declared in full |
| Add settings of this theme's own | `extension.json`, with a `type` and a `label` |

The build finds {{parentName}} in the panel's extensions directory (`extensions` in `vite.config.mjs`), else in
`node_modules`, and builds its stylesheet and classes in after the panel's, so `src/theme.css` stays one import
plus your own rules. Rebuild after {{parentName}} changes.

## Develop

```sh
npm install
php {{artisan}} p:extension:dev . --enable
php {{artisan}} p:theme:activate {{id}}
php {{artisan}} p:extension:dev . --watch
```
